{{Term/Store|Thunder Wizzrobe|Thunder Wizzrobes|Series, BotW, TotK, AoC|plural}} are recurring [[Boss]]es and [[Enemy|Enemies]] in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref>{{Cite|'''Thunder Wizzrobe'''|Hyrule Compendium|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|'''Thunder Wizzrobe'''|Hyrule Compendium|TotK}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Big|'''Thunder Wizzrobe'''}}|Game Screen|AoC}}</ref>

==Characteristics==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract|Thunder Wizzrobe}}
Thunder Wizzrobes are a variant of [[Electric Wizzrobe]]s. They attack by using their [[Thunderstorm Rod]]s to cast three balls of electricity, to summon [[Electric Chuchu]]s and [[Electric Keese]], as well as to summon thunderstorms that will strike [[Link]] if he is wielding any metallic [[Weapon]].<ref>{{Cite|They use their thunderstorm rods to hurl balls of electricity or to summon monsters surging with electricity and have been known to cause thunderstorms in the area.|Hyrule Compendium|BotW}}</ref> Thunder Wizzrobes will turn invisible after attacking, however, they leave trails below them. Performing a headshot will stun them, giving Link time to attack. After defeat, they will drop their Thunderstorm Rods.

==={{TotK|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract/TotK|Thunder Wizzrobe}}
{{Stub|TotK}}
Instead of a [[Thunderstorm Rod]], Thunder Wizzrobes now carry a [[Magic Rod]] that has been [[Fuse]]d to a [[Topaz]].

==Other Appearances==
==={{AoC|-}}===
{{Noncanon|Start}}
{{Stub|AoC}}
Thunder Wizzrobes appear as [[Powerful Foe]]s in the {{PotA}} Downloadable Content pack for {{AoC}}, fighting with stronger attacks, such as firing electric magic blasts in a spinning motion.
{{Noncanon|End}}

